{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/50035-questions-and-theories-on-the-fae-workings-of-iron","id":50035,"title":"Questions and Theories on the fae Workings of Iron","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-15T13:36:22-08:00","id":50035,"title":"Questions and Theories on the fae Workings of Iron","content":"So first are my questions because they are starting to become very relevant in a game that I am running.<br /> <br /> Things I know based on reading the books:<br /> <b>Cold Iron </b>counts as: Any amounts of Iron ore that has not been touched by human heat (enough heat that changes to properties at least). This means: Pure Iron ingots (well pure enough to be called Iron instead of steel or otherwise), Meteoric Iron, or Telluric Iron. Any of these will cause aggravated damage to the True Fae and cut through fae enchantments.<br /> <br /> <b>Pure Iron</b> counts as: Iron that has been touched by human heat (significant enough to change it's properties) and is pure enough to be called iron instead of say steel. This means: Iron pokers, Cast Iron Skillets, or Iron fence posts. Any of these will not cause aggravated damage to the True Fae but <u>will</u> cut through fae enchantments.<br /> <br /> <br /> My questions are:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Will <b>Cold Iron</b> do aggravated damage if it simply touches the Fae or does it at least have to do 1 bashing damage?</li> <li>When it says &quot;cut through all fae enchantments&quot; does that mean all contracts and fae magic? Like if someone is using a contract to be invisible, being cut by a Pure Iron knife will make them visible? If they are growing thorny vines via a contract will cutting the vines be both very easy and cancel the contract? Will cutting an object granted by a vow make the vow invalid? I'm worried that if I allow Iron to be found, that it will be basically anti-changeling. That anything anyone does can be negated by a piece of Iron.</li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T13:55:53-08:00","id":50049,"title":"","content":"1: It has to do at least 1 Bashing Damange<br /> 2: I always read that as it ignores any Contract or other Fae Magic that would make it harder to do damage. Turn into air, magic faerie suit of armour, useless against Iron. I'm not sure whether giving yourself super-speed and using it to dodge would work against iron or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T14:24:34-08:00","id":50075,"title":"","content":"<b><i>NOTE: The following is how I interpret the use of iron in the games that I organize and run. It is not, by any means, &quot;canon.&quot;</i></b><br /> <br /> I interpret the subject of your second question a bit more liberally than The Kings Raven, although his implementation of the rule is not incorrect. I take it to mean that iron, when used in the appropriate context, is an effective bane to <b>all </b>fairy enchantments. For Example, if a changeling is bound in iron shackles, her Mask will fall away (it is an illusion crafted of Glamour, after all) and she will be unable to utilize her Kith and Seeming blessings as well as her Contracts. This is not to say that Iron is some sort of &quot;anti&quot; magic sorta allergy thing. It isn't like if a changeling tripped and stumbled into an iron fence his Mask would shatter and he would lose all of his magical protections. Rather, it is about the *intent* of the Iron in question that nullifies the specific enchantments.<br /> <br /> An iron ring, when looked through, would nullify fairy magic that aided in Stealth and would reveal the Mask. An iron capped cudgel would shatter fairy armor and toughness. An iron cross, when worn against the skin, would protect the wearer from ensorcellment and clauses that befuddled the senses. An iron bell, when rung would rouse someone locked in an enchanted slumber. etc etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","user":"Firefly Night","date":". 01-15-2014, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T15:04:53-08:00","id":50126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firefly Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/50035-questions-and-theories-on-the-fae-workings-of-iron?p=50075#post50075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I interpret the subject of your second question a bit more liberally than The Kings Raven, although his implementation of the rule is not incorrect. I take it to mean that iron, when used in the appropriate context, is an effective bane to <b>all </b>fairy enchantments. For Example, if a changeling is bound in iron shackles, her Mask will fall away (it is an illusion crafted of Glamour, after all) and she will be unable to utilize her Kith and Seeming blessings as well as her Contracts. This is not to say that Iron is some sort of &quot;anti&quot; magic sorta allergy thing. It isn't like if a changeling tripped and stumbled into an iron fence his Mask would shatter and he would lose all of his magical protections. Rather, it is about the *intent* of the Iron in question that nullifies the specific enchantments.<br /> <br /> An iron ring, when looked through, would nullify fairy magic that aided in Stealth and would reveal the Mask. An iron capped cudgel would shatter fairy armor and toughness. An iron cross, when worn against the skin, would protect the wearer from ensorcellment and clauses that befuddled the senses. An iron bell, when rung would rouse someone locked in an enchanted slumber. etc etc<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Your interpretation is well beyond what the core says. It specifies &quot;defenses&quot; from Contracts and fae magic, not Contracts and fae magic in general. If it was that far reaching, it would have been spelled out with more explicit language and examples than a Contract and some fae armor.<br /> <br /> And you made me side with KR <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> - bad lightning bug, no cookie","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1651-phalamir","name":"phalamir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T15:09:51-08:00","id":50134,"title":"","content":"As I said, it is a very liberal interpretation of the rules. I wasn't trying to contradict what King's Raven said, in fact, I said he wasn't incorrect. Which means he is right. What you read, and what I had I hoped I had gotten across with my collection of words, is how I *personally* use iron. I am sorry if I wasn't more clear. Let me go back and add a disclaimer to the original post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T15:18:40-08:00","id":50143,"title":"","content":"The big thing is that your interpretation makes iron wildly more problematic for changelings. Everyone and his little brother knows the tidbit that iron screws faeries. As-is, iron sits about where o/nWoD wooden stakes does for vampires - technically correct as a bane, but grossly over-wrought in the man on the street's perceptions. Increase its power to where it is a Dispel Magic for changelings, and you would be insane not to buy-out Lodge's entire warehouse to chunk griddles and Dutch ovens at changelings willy-nilly.<br /> <br /> PS the &quot;bad lightning bug, no cookie&quot; was for making me side with KR","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1651-phalamir","name":"phalamir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T15:39:59-08:00","id":50170,"title":"","content":"Again, I am afraid that my collection of words did not impart the information that I wished to convey. Iron in my games, is not &quot;Dispel Magic&quot; against fairies. As I had stated, a changeling who trips and falls into an iron gate does not lose any of their glamorous protections. Iron is effective against fairy magic because at some point in the distant past, some sort of agreement or other such fairy nonsense decided that it would be the case. It is not really about the physical or chemical composition of the Iron that acts as a ward against glamour, it is about the *intent* of the iron that acts as a bane.<br /> <br /> So, a police officer's steel handcuffs bind the changeling as effectively as any other manner in which a person is restrained. A set of &quot;cold&quot; heavy iron shackles that some old woman sold you from the back of her van, which she claims once bound a lamia for a thousand years? Well, that will strip a changeling of their fairy magic and Mask. See the difference? The handcuffs don't have the weight of narrative or myth backing it. &quot;Cold&quot; Iron (even though it really isn't even a thing) is a product of fairy tale logic ... which really is the only sort of logic that fairies have. <br /> <br /> Have I made myself clear? Throwing an iron nail at a fairy is not going to kill it. However, if you sleep in a bed that has that Iron nail pounded into the headboard ... it will keep a fairy from manipulating your dreams while you sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T17:02:15-08:00","id":51194,"title":"","content":"I very much like the author Kevin hearn's interpritation. In the Iron Druid series of movels, Mr. Hearn claims that to be truly &quot;cold iron&quot; the metal had to come from a meteorite (i.e. not of earth).<br /> <br /> As I imagine most, if not all, contracts are somehow ingerently tied to the natural world, having something basically alien to that world being able to thwart those contracts just makes sense to me. Plus, from a more mechanical POV, meteorite iron is super rare, so it limits the amount players should reasonably expect to come across. As an added bonus from a player perspective, the PCs can still intersect with surgical tool, cutlery, fences, etc. without having to constantly check if the magic is working and it gets around having to reseach hott forge bs cold forge tempuraters and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I also post a long form story, based on a Changeling: The Lost campaign at: <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10018173/1/Great-Fight-A-Twilight-Tommy-Tale\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.fanfiction.net/s/1001817...ght-Tommy-Tale</a><br /> I hope you will enjoy it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2020-gitariart","name":"GitariArt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T17:51:46-08:00","id":51236,"title":"","content":"So far, for the purposes of my game I am going to go with The Kings Raven's interpretation. It meshes pretty naturally with how my chronicle is going. However I am still open to more interpretations if anyone has them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T01:54:51-08:00","id":52229,"title":"","content":"Ah...who was it that wrote how faeries could only be hurt by cold iron, in the same way that you have to warm up your bullets first, because gangsters were vulnerable to hot lead?<br /> <br /> anyways...<br /> <br /> I don't have the books on me to quote specifics, but I generally consider Iron to be proof against fae magic and crafts <i>if it is the object's nature to do so in that situation.</i> <br /> <br /> An iron sword cuts fae armor easily. Iron shackles won't unlock at their command, nor can they wriggle out of them. iron armor turns fae blades aside with ease. <br /> <br /> In a straight match between troll and Iron door, the door wins - because it's job is to keep things out. <br /> <br /> The fae are expert rules-lawyers, and will instead work <i>around </i>the obstacle. The fae lures the opponent into a trap, instead of attacking the knight covered head-to-toe in armor. The fae disguises himself and tricks someone to unlock the shackles, etc.<br /> <br /> And having an Iron door doesn't mean the troll can't break through the window, or that you can make fae-made things explode just by poking them with a piece of iron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T11:40:26-08:00","id":57546,"title":"","content":"Strange that no one has brought this up yet:<br /> <br /> In the story in Winter Masques a Moon Court changeling is about to be tortured by &quot;true iron, not steel, and cold forged&quot;, His torturer has to wear gloves, because &quot;he fared no better than Veles under the touch of cold iron.&quot; Veles panics, because he can't &quot;afford to let the iron touch his flesh - would cut through false seemings and goblin magics as easily as skin.&quot;<br /> <br /> For those who don't have the book, Veles in story is a Sun court spymaster in a disguise in order to create a casus belli between courts, so he has to look as a known member of Moon court.<br /> <br /> So at least according to that story, cold iron goes through everything you can define as fae magic defenses. Armor, defense upgrades, stealth and illusions made to protect your true self.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2095,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2095-daider-santo","user":"Daider Santo","date":". 01-26-2014, 06:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2095-daider-santo","name":"Daider Santo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T11:56:19-08:00","id":58224,"title":"","content":"The same piece of fiction allows Veles to swear an oath in another's name, though, and let that person suffer the consequences of breaking it.<br /> It kind of plays fast and loose with the rules, to say the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T01:45:53-08:00","id":58587,"title":"","content":"They way I see it Veles only thinks he can do it, because of his goblin magic (rules vs fluff). Who knows, maybe there is a goblin contract that allows you to pass the burden of oath to someone else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2095-daider-santo","name":"Daider Santo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T09:19:05-08:00","id":58775,"title":"","content":"Two things I want to point out.<br /> One, it does specifically say iron weapons can go through worn fae armor (I imagine this refers to hedgespun stuff). Specifically it says, &quot;A changeling wearing fae armor will find it's no protection from a spike torn from a wrought iron fence.&quot;<br /> Two, cold iron cannot be transmuted, conjured, or shaped by magic. If it is, it's not cold iron, and just iron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T00:52:03-08:00","id":59599,"title":"","content":"One: &quot;...an item made from relatively pure iron (not steel) ignores defenses contrived by the fae and their magics.&quot; CtL 174. Where is your quote from?<br /> Two: That is hand forged iron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2095-daider-santo","name":"Daider Santo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T10:26:17-08:00","id":59936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daider Santo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/50035-questions-and-theories-on-the-fae-workings-of-iron?p=59599#post59599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One: &quot;...an item made from relatively pure iron (not steel) ignores defenses contrived by the fae and their magics.&quot; CtL 174. Where is your quote from?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Cold Iron,&quot; corebook, page 174, top of the second column.<br /> <br /> From same: &quot;Mass-produced, machine-cut knives are not 'cold iron,' nor is metal that has been conjured, transmuted or even shaped by magic.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T12:51:48-08:00","id":60058,"title":"","content":"I guess the reason I prefer an application of Iron along the lines of what myself and QuantumShard stated earlier is just how stupid and arbitrary the definition of &quot;cold iron&quot; is. So, is blood (which has a high concentration of iron) anathema to fairies? Or does the act of it being circulated through the human body negate its fairy-bane properties because it was &quot;heated&quot; by human metabolism? Then how about pig blood? How about ochre?<br /> <br /> I mean, in folklore it is said that iron horseshoes hung above your door keeps the fairies away. Horseshoes aren't &quot;cold forged&quot; or crafted without the application of human supplied heat. But then again, that is a folklore thing ... why on Earth would the game designers use that as an inspiration instead of this weird new age throwback that is more reminiscent of Kryptonite than fairy taboos?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T03:08:32-08:00","id":60610,"title":"","content":"My bad for reading the column too fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2095-daider-santo","name":"Daider Santo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T15:42:26-08:00","id":61120,"title":"","content":"I'll have to get the quote from the book once I'm home from work but Cold-Iron is more specified in the Spring book. It says that Cold Iron is Iron that is &quot;pure&quot; enough to be called iron (as opposed to steel or blood) <b>and </b>has not been touched by human heat (as in intentionally heated to a degree that changes it's properties (so no forging).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T16:59:21-08:00","id":61167,"title":"","content":"My point is that &quot;cold iron,&quot; in real life, is just a poetic description. Like &quot;Cold Steel&quot; or &quot;Hot Lead&quot; or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T17:47:29-08:00","id":61192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firefly Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/50035-questions-and-theories-on-the-fae-workings-of-iron?p=61167#post61167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is that &quot;cold iron,&quot; in real life, is just a poetic description. Like &quot;Cold Steel&quot; or &quot;Hot Lead&quot; or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your point is incoherent, seeing as the definition of cold iron that Changeling uses is &quot;generally referred to as iron rather than by a different name, shaped by human toil rather than by magic&quot; and babbling about blood and new-age Kryptonite when the system is by necessity going to have to address what counts as iron when iron is on the Periodic Table as an only-rarely-pure substance doesn't endear your perspective.<br /> <br /> That you cite Quantumshard's citation of the Dresden Files does little to help with this, given that Butcher's fairies can be and have been done harm by nail guns.<br /> <br /> You can ramble about stupidity and arbitrariness elsewhere. Quit shitting up the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T18:08:36-08:00","id":61200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/50035-questions-and-theories-on-the-fae-workings-of-iron?p=61192#post61192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can ramble about stupidity and arbitrariness elsewhere. Quit shitting up the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firefly Nights oppinions are as valid as yours, more so since he clearly has done some research.<br /> Even I have access to wikipedia: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cold_iron#Cold_iron\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cold_iron#Cold_iron</a><br /> If the rule books were clear enough to rely on with no other referenses, then there would be no need for this forum in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I also post a long form story, based on a Changeling: The Lost campaign at: <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10018173/1/Great-Fight-A-Twilight-Tommy-Tale\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.fanfiction.net/s/1001817...ght-Tommy-Tale</a><br /> I hope you will enjoy it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2020-gitariart","name":"GitariArt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T18:12:28-08:00","id":61204,"title":"","content":"Satchel: Who crowned you regent? You didn't start this thread, and even if you did, it's no excuse for being rude to Firefly Night. It's unfortunate that you do not understand the point he is making so you are getting angry. I'm pretty sure that point of the forum is for people to share opinions and help each other figure out rules (since the books are labyrinthine). We are not here to all agree to one universal truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2002-quynce","name":"Quynce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2002_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T18:24:31-08:00","id":61217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GitariArt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/50035-questions-and-theories-on-the-fae-workings-of-iron?p=61200#post61200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Firefly Nights oppinions are as valid as yours, more so since he clearly has done some research.<br /> Even I have access to wikipedia: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cold_iron#Cold_iron\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cold_iron#Cold_iron</a><br /> If the rule books were clear enough to rely on with no other referenses, then there would be no need for this forum in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rites of Spring duplicates many of the effects being forwarded and I would advise you not to talk to someone who is literally reading through as much of the WoD as possible about doing their research.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quynce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/50035-questions-and-theories-on-the-fae-workings-of-iron?p=61204#post61204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Satchel: Who crowned you regent?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't need a royal seal to advise someone to know when they're wearing out the bounds of polite speech.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You didn't start this thread, and even if you did, it's no excuse for being rude to Firefly Night. </div> </div> </div>I do not need to be the one who started a thread to find the way people express their opinions obnoxious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's unfortunate that you do not understand the point he is making so you are getting angry. </div> </div> </div>I have been in too many long, pointless arguments to appreciate seeing the hallmarks of one in the making. Night's the one making the bulk of the posts pushing it toward one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm pretty sure that point of the forum is for people to share opinions and help each other figure out rules (since the books are labyrinthine). We are not here to all agree to one universal truth. </div> </div> </div>Opinions have been shared. Helping has occurred. What Night is doing at this point has ceased to be either. You were saying something about understanding points?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T20:49:13-08:00","id":61282,"title":"","content":"Alright guys, I am out! I didn't mean to upset anyone with my ideas! Have fun with your discussion!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T04:11:30-08:00","id":61452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firefly Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/50035-questions-and-theories-on-the-fae-workings-of-iron?p=61282#post61282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright guys, I am out! I didn't mean to upset anyone with my ideas! Have fun with your discussion!</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, another bully has won and driven off someone they did not life. More than one, for I tii an iyt,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I also post a long form story, based on a Changeling: The Lost campaign at: <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10018173/1/Great-Fight-A-Twilight-Tommy-Tale\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.fanfiction.net/s/1001817...ght-Tommy-Tale</a><br /> I hope you will enjoy it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2020-gitariart","name":"GitariArt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T11:19:16-08:00","id":61631,"title":"","content":"Reviewing the information so far I think I am going to go with a more restrictive view on how Iron works. At least for this game that I am running. The themes of this chronicle highlight on the feelings of powerlessness and focus on crafty 'fae' like workings and powers. I want truly formidable iron to feel like the Holy Grail and for it to be a significant portion of the story. <br /> <br /> So while it's not the only way to view how Cold Iron works, it's the one that fits most with the themes for this specific chronicle.<br /> <br /> I'd still be interested in hearing more opinions though. And I'd be glad to respond with how it was used in game and how the players took it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}